Package: cehbio
Title: UKCEH Biomonitoring Toolkit from R
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R: person("Alyssa", "Duffy", email = "alyduf@ceh.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Use the UKCEH ceh-biomonitoring toolkit entirely from R: install it, run the bird, bat
    and moth-trap pipelines, follow their progress, read the results, and make summary reports. The
    models themselves run in the toolkit's Python environment, which this package sets up and drives,
    so R users never need to write Python. The report tables and reports are made in R, with no Python
    needed, by the same rules as the toolkit's Python reports, so both give the same numbers.
